WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.762
Here's what Microsoft gives you.

2
00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:05.741
Two Learn pages walk through
creating a federated credential,

3
00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:10.333
one for an app registration and one
for a user-assigned managed identity,

4
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:14.924
with samples in the command line,
PowerShell, a template and raw requests.

5
00:00:14.924 --> 00:00:17.480
Graph's reference has
its own create request,

6
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.725
and the managed identity
reference has worked examples.

7
00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:25.443
All of that lives only inside web pages,
so the repository pins the sources

8
00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:27.841
unmodified, with hashes a test checks,

9
00:00:27.841 --> 00:00:31.012
and a weekly watch that
reports upstream changes.

10
00:00:31.012 --> 00:00:33.992
A harness then runs every
sample against fakes,

11
00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:36.500
so you can see what each one really does.
